    <div class="faq-list">
      <details class="faq-item" open>
        <summary class="faq-question">Google Drive says "Download quota exceeded for this file". How to fix?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>This is Google Drive's bandwidth security limit when thousands of users download the same file simultaneously. You have two easy solutions:</p>
          <ol>
            <li><strong>Use the "Fast Cloud" or "Download Links" button:</strong> These mirror servers do not have Google quota restrictions.</li>
            <li><strong>Bypass on Google Drive:</strong> Click the three dots on the top right of Google Drive &gt; <em>Add shortcut to Drive</em> &gt; Open your own Google Drive &gt; Right-click the shortcut and select <em>Make a copy</em> &gt; Download the copy!</li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-question">There is no sound / audio when playing the movie on my Smart TV or phone.</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>This happens when your default TV or phone media player does not support Dolby Digital (AC3, E-AC3, or DTS 5.1) codecs. Simply install <strong>VLC Media Player</strong> or <strong>Kodi</strong> on your Smart TV/Android device; VLC has built-in decoders for every audio codec.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-question">How do I download complete Web Series seasons at once?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>For Web Series, we provide both <strong>Complete Season Zip Packs</strong> (one single archive containing all episodes) and individual episode links. Look for the tier labeled <em>[Complete Season 1 Zip Pack]</em> in the download section.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-question">The download says "File is in RAR or ZIP format". How do I extract it?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>Download and install <strong>7-Zip</strong> or <strong>WinRAR</strong> on PC, or <strong>ZArchiver</strong> from the Google Play Store on Android. Right-click or tap the downloaded archive and select <em>Extract Here</em> to get the MKV video file.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

